<section class="safari-more-details">
    <div class="container">
        <h3>Sunset Experience in Amaltari</h3>
        <p>
            Witness the breathtaking beauty of the sun dipping below the horizon, casting golden reflections over the Narayani River and the lush forest edge of Chitwan National Park. The sunset in Amaltari is a serene experience that invites calmness and awe, offering the perfect way to conclude a day of exploration.
        </p>

        <h3>Sunset Viewpoints</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Narayani Riverbank:</strong> The most popular spot, where the river mirrors the changing colors of the sky.</li>
            <li><strong>Machan Viewpoints:</strong> Elevated platforms offer an uninterrupted panoramic view of the forest and river.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Timing & Duration</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Ideal Time:</strong> Between 5:30 PM – 6:30 PM (varies by season)</li>
            <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Around 30–45 minutes of prime viewing</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What to Expect</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>A peaceful and scenic setting surrounded by water, forest, and occasional wildlife sightings</li>
            <li>Opportunities for stunning landscape photography and reflection</li>
            <li>Sound of birds returning to their nests, with gentle breezes and the calm flow of the river</li>
            <li>Small seating areas or benches available at certain viewpoints</li>
            <li><strong>Light local snacks and tea are provided while waiting for the sunset</strong>, adding to the comfort and experience</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Additional Tips</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Arrive 15 minutes early to secure the best view</li>
            <li>Carry a light jacket during winter months as it can get cool</li>
            <li>Respect nature—avoid loud noise and littering at the viewpoint</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Why It’s Special</h3>
        <p>
            Sunset viewing in Amaltari is not just about scenic beauty—it’s a moment of connection with nature, offering tranquility and reflection after a day full of adventures. The colors, the sounds, and the peaceful atmosphere make it one of the most cherished parts of the visitor experience.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>





